{title: 456 - My Lord and I}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #456 • MY LORD AND I • 12.16.14.11}
{lyricist: Mary Ann Shorey}
{composer: Hubert P. Main}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 456}
{meta: tune MY LORD AND I}
{meta: meter 12.16.14.11}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]I [Bb/F]have [F]a Friend so precious, [Dm/A]So [Bb]very dear tome,
[F]He loves me with a [C7/E]tender [F]love, He loves [Dm]so [Gm]faithfully;
[F]I [C7/G]could not [Am]live [C7/E]apart [F]from [Dm]Him, Ilove to [C]feel [F]Him nigh;
[Bb/F]And so [F]we dwell together, My [C7]Lord and [F]I.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Sometimes I'm [Dm/A]faint [Bb]and weary,
[F]He knows that [Dm]I [Bb]am weak,
[F]And [Bb/F]as [F]He [C7/E]bids [F]me lean [Dm]on [Gm]Him,
[F]His help I gladly [Gm]seek;
[F]He [C7/Bb]leads me in [Dm]the paths [Gm]of [F]light,
[F]Beneath [C7/E]a [Dm]sunny [F]sky,
[Bb/F]And [F]so we walk together,
[Bb/F]My [F]Lord and [C7]I.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]I [Bb/F]tell [F]Him all [Dm/A]my [Bb]sorrows,
[F]I tell Him [Dm]all [Bb]my joys,
[F]I [Bb/F]tell [F]Him [C7/E]all [F]that pleases [Gm]me,
[F]I tell Him what [Dm]annoys;
[F]He [C7/Bb]tells me what [Dm]I ought [Gm]to [F]do,
[F]He [Am]tells [C7/E]me [Dm]how to [F]try,
[Bb/F]And [F]so we talk together,
[Bb/F]My [F]Lord and [C7]I.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]He [Bb/F]knows [F]that I [Dm/A]am [Bb]longing
[F]Some weary [Dm]soul [Bb]to win,
[F]And [Bb/F]so [F]He [C7/E]bids [F]me go [Dm]and [Gm]speak
[F]The loving word [Dm]for [Gm]Him;
[F]He [C7/Bb]bids me tell [Dm]His wondrous [F]love,
[F]And [Am]why [C7/E]He [Dm]came to [F]die,
[Bb/F]And [F]so we work together,
[Bb/F]My [F]Lord and [C7]I.
{end_of_verse}
